    "content": "---\n\n> **PAGE:** `/platforms/oracle/`  \n> **SOURCE FILE:** `wave1-generated/platforms/oracle.md`\n\n\n\n\n# Oracle Development Services\n\n**Oracle estates demand respect and exit-awareness — we extend, integrate, and where the math says so, help you leave.** Clickmasters works on Oracle for US businesses — and because we also build custom software, our platform advice carries no allegiance: configure, extend, or exit, priced side by side, decided by your numbers.\n\n[Trust bar: [PLACEHOLDER]]\n\n## Our Oracle Services\n\n- **Integration to Oracle ERP/DB estates**\n- **Reporting layers over Oracle data**\n- **Migration assessments with license math**\n- **[Integration development](/services/api-development/)** — Oracle connected to the rest of your company with reconciliation discipline\n- **Rescue & rationalization** — inherited implementations audited, de-bloated, stabilized\n\n## The Boundary Read\n\nEvery platform has edges: inside them, configuration beats code and we'll say so; at them, custom development makes the platform earn its fees; past them, the [exit conversation](/frameworks/build-vs-buy/) deserves real numbers. The first deliverable of any Oracle engagement is that boundary read for your implementation, in writing.\n\n## Recent Oracle Work\n\n> **[PLACEHOLDER — 1–2 verifiable case studies. Required before indexing.]**\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Should we customize Oracle or replace it?**\nThe assessment prices rationalize / extend / exit side by side against your renewal and usage reality — the answer is arithmetic, not allegiance.\n\n**Can you connect Oracle to our other systems?**\nThat's usually the center of the work: bidirectional sync with field-mapping sign-off, idempotent operations, and daily reconciliation reports.\n\n**Our implementation is a mess. Can it be rescued?**\nAlmost always — the audit maps the debt, the rationalization pass consolidates it, and everything after gets cheaper. It's the highest-ROI platform work nobody sells.\n\n**What does platform work cost?**\nAssessments: [PLACEHOLDER fixed fee]. Integration and customization projects scoped fixed-milestone — see [cost guides](/resources/software-cost-guides/).\n\n**How fast can work start?**\nAssessments within 1–2 weeks; project kickoffs typically within 2 weeks of scope sign-off.\n\n---\n\n### Book a Oracle Assessment\nBring the implementation and its invoices — leave with the boundary read and three paths priced.\n[Form] [Calendar embed]",
